@vsm 1.2.1
@status ratified
// s5-policy/vsl-language/encyclopedia.vsm — encyclopedia build spec (§20).
// Source: vsl_language §20 (encyclopedia/spec.vsm). Item of the reference
// set. PRESENTATION layer of the canon, not new authority.

encyclopedia("VSL-LANG-ENCYCLOPEDIA") {

  encyclopedia: "
    purpose: public, curated, bilingual (ES/EN), cross-linked encyclopedia of
      VSF+VSM — PRESENTATION layer of canon, not new authority. audience: Beer
      community + newcomers. derives from glossary.vsm.
    D1: authorship us, from canon, via git/PR — no wiki/no browser editing (SSG)
    D2: glossary.vsm IS canon; entries DERIVE, not parallel authority; new term
      enters glossary FIRST
    D3: no db as source — search index is DERIVED artifact; no git = no canon
    D4: output static HTML, zero runtime surface (coherent w/ theme D)
    D5: wiki SPIRIT (dense hyperlinks) without wiki engine — encyclopedia =
      MAP of the whole model; references field typed + coverage metric
    architecture: FUENTE (git, glossary.vsm + entries/*.yaml) → reconciler →
      index (search.json, generated) → aphid.py → VISTA (static HTML)
      // layers regenerated from source; never hand-edited
    entry_schema: slug, canon_ref (→ glossary term, OBLIGATORY), category,
      formal (VERBATIM from glossary — reconciler enforces equality),
      aliases[], see_also[] (concept→concept), certainty ∈ { canonical,
      vsf-extension, interpretation, open }, references[] (concept→artifact),
      term{es,en}, one_line{es,en}, body{es,en}, boundary{es,en}
      // i18n: all prose {es,en}; 'en' may be explicit TODO
    reference_taxonomy: concept | code(file::symbol) | paper(§) | spec |
      experiment(EXP-*) | axiom | service(state.db) | literature
    reconciler checks (build fails on red): 1 INTEGRITY (canon_ref real)
      2 FORMAL-EQ (formal verbatim) 3 COVERAGE (terms no entry, WARN)
      4 I18N (prose {es,en}, WARN TODO) 5 LINKS (see_also exists)
      6 STALE-CANON (REVERSE: glossary says pending but code LIVE → update
      glossary — encyclopedia AUDITS canon) 7 REF-INTEGRITY (refs resolve,
      anti-orphan) 8 ARTIFACT-COVERAGE (orphan artifacts report, WARN —
      the D5 progress bar)
    build: aphid.py (port of Aphid v1.0 TreeOfContents, MIT) — render static,
      escaping (not XSS class); body authoring in MARKDOWN (markdown-it-py AST
      + TreeOfContents as renderer — reuse parser, port renderer, not hand-rolled)
    taxonomy: vsm-beer | cybersyn | vos-kernel | vos-theory | axioms |
      governance | infra
    phases: P1 nucleus Beer (~15 terms) → P2 vOS corpus (~25) → P3 enrichment
      (boundary/certainty/refs full; EN full; coverage complete)
    gate: not implement until (1) rmw3 ratifies (2) LEDGER-DEAF-P3 arc closes",
}
⟦ /encyclopedia ⟧